Reason: every enemy's begin step calls instance_activate_region on the 64×64 square around itself, after Samus's
begin step has put the far solids to sleep and woken the ones near the view, and each call walked every instance in
the room working out the box of each one that sits out (about 0.18 ms a call on the real Wii in rm_a5h04). The
inactive instances are now kept in room order and bucketed by box over the collision grid's cells; a call tests
only those in the cells it covers, in room order, with the same test as before. The index is rebuilt whenever the
runner's activation version (any instance turning active or inactive, any change to the instance list) or the
grid's count of edits to sitting-out instances has moved since; Samus's own begin step moves it, so that is about
once a frame, which costs more than it saves in rooms under 300 instances: those, and a region that is inverted,
huge, or asks for the outside, walk the room as before. On the Wii: rm_a5h04 1.03–1.08 → 0.55–0.67 ms a frame,
rm_a2h02 0.93 → 0.35.
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

